# Customer Meeting - Requirements

The following requirements were discussed and agreed upon during the client meeting for the Payment Processing Platform.

## Dashboard
- Provide a dashboard to manage all payment activities.
- Allow users to initiate payments to vendors.
- Display payment status and transaction history.
- Generate proof of successful payments.

## Vendor Management
- Allow users to add new vendors.
- Store vendor information for future payments.

## Payment Management
- Create payments to registered vendors.
- Store payment details including:
  - Payment amount
  - Sender account
  - Receiver account
  - Date and time
  - Payment status
- Track the complete payment lifecycle from creation to completion or failure.

## Invoice-Based Payments
- Every payment must be linked to an invoice.
- Each invoice should have only one successful payment.
- Prevent duplicate payments for the same invoice.
- If a payment is pending, another payment for the same invoice should not be allowed.
- If a payment fails, the invoice should be available for payment again.

## Retry Handling
- Retry failed payments automatically when appropriate.
- Ensure vendors are not paid twice due to retry attempts.
- Allow retries only after confirming that the previous payment has failed.

## Multi-Currency Support
- Support payments to international vendors.
- Convert currencies using the latest exchange rate.
- Support payments from INR to foreign currencies (e.g., GBP).
- Include applicable Forex charges during currency conversion.
- Apply Forex deductions for international transactions.

## Reporting & Audit
- Maintain complete payment history.
- Allow users to search payments by vendor, date, amount, and status.
- Generate payment reports.
- Keep an audit trail of all payment activities.

## Error Handling
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes for successful and failed requests.
- Display meaningful error messages for validation failures, duplicate payments, and processing errors.

##Refund Handling and payment adjustment
 -Detect overpayments and underpayments against invoices
 -Allow refund processing through dashboard
 -Also option to adjust excess payment against future invoices
 
